#V  PRIMGRP_SIMSNO
##
##  Sims' numbering of the primitive groups of degree at most 50.  It orders
##  the same groups differently, so PRIMGRP_SIMSNO[deg-1][nr] is Sims' number
##  for PrimitiveGroup(deg,nr), and it is not the identity: 113 of these 406
##  numbers differ from nr.  Small enough to keep here rather than as a tenth
##  field on every entry of PRIMGRP.
##
